---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Navbar from '../components/Navbar.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import { SITE_GITHUB_URL } from '../constants';
---

<Layout
  title="Terms of Service — Kery"
  description="Terms of use for kery.dev and notices regarding the Kery open-source software."
>
  <Navbar />
  <main class="legal-page">
    <div class="container legal-inner">
      <h1>Terms of Service</h1>
      <p class="legal-updated">Last updated: April 4, 2026</p>

      <h2>1. Agreement</h2>
      <p>
        By accessing <strong>kery.dev</strong> (“Site”), you agree to these Terms. If you do not agree, do not use the
        Site.
      </p>

      <h2>2. Software license</h2>
      <p>
        The Kery software is distributed under the <strong>Apache License, Version 2.0</strong>. Your use, reproduction,
        and distribution of the code are governed by that license, not by these Terms. A copy of the license ships
        with the repository at <a href={SITE_GITHUB_URL}>GitHub</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>3. Site content</h2>
      <p>
        Marketing copy, branding, and design assets on the Site are owned by the Kery project or its contributors
        and are provided for informational purposes. You may link to the Site; do not misrepresent affiliation or
        endorsements.
      </p>

      <h2>4. No warranty</h2>
      <p>
        THE SITE AND ANY DOCUMENTATION ARE PROVIDED “AS IS” WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR IMPLIED,
        INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY, FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE, OR
        NON-INFRINGEMENT. AI-assisted testing can miss issues or report false positives; you remain responsible for
        your release process.
      </p>

      <h2>5. Limitation of liability</h2>
      <p>
        TO THE MAXIMUM EXTENT PERMITTED BY LAW, IN NO EVENT SHALL THE CONTRIBUTORS OR COPYRIGHT HOLDERS BE LIABLE FOR
        ANY INDIRECT, INCIDENTAL, SPECIAL, CONSEQUENTIAL, OR PUNITIVE DAMAGES, OR ANY LOSS OF PROFITS, DATA, OR
        GOODWILL, ARISING OUT OF OR RELATED TO YOUR USE OF THE SITE OR THE SOFTWARE, WHETHER BASED IN CONTRACT,
        TORT, OR ANY OTHER LEGAL THEORY, EVEN IF ADVISED OF THE POSSIBILITY OF SUCH DAMAGES.
      </p>

      <h2>6. Future hosted services</h2>
      <p>
        If Kery offers a managed cloud product, it will be subject to separate terms of service and, where applicable,
        a commercial agreement. These Site terms apply only to the marketing website and general OSS distribution
        unless otherwise stated.
      </p>

      <h2>7. Changes</h2>
      <p>
        We may modify these Terms. The “Last updated” date will change when we do; continued use of the Site after
        changes constitutes acceptance of the revised Terms.
      </p>

      <h2>8. Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Reach the maintainers via the
        <a href={SITE_GITHUB_URL}>Kery GitHub repository</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Layout>

<style>
  .legal-page {
    padding-top: 6rem;
    padding-bottom: var(--space-2xl);
    min-height: 60vh;
  }

  .legal-inner {
    max-width: 720px;
  }

  .legal-inner h1 {
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }

  .legal-updated {
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-lg);
  }

  .legal-inner h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    margin-top: var(--space-lg);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-sm);
    color: var(--color-text);
  }

  .legal-inner p {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-sm);
    font-size: 1rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .legal-inner a {
    color: var(--color-accent);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 2px;
  }

  .legal-inner a:hover {
    color: var(--color-accent-hover);
  }
</style>
